From 75eed6470d6ea572dedeed40bc4403d5ff124185 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:13:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] WIP: Quick Share engine: registration fails the protocol,
 fair peer table, progress deadline

receive::start registers the announcement before it returns, so a
refusal shows as Quick Share failing. The peer table lists at most four
peers per source (the packets' source, from mdns-sd), a newcomer at a
full table replacing the oldest of the source listing the most, and an id
stays its source's; announcements are rate-limited on a budget of Quick
Share's own, keyed on the source. After acceptance the sender must make
progress within the idle limit: keep-alives and empty chunks no longer
hold a transfer open. Tests: a real registration resolved by a second
daemon, a flood that leaves a phone listable, the table's policy, and a
sender that only keeps talking.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ENZSCiAud5Vs29ugEacpyR
